From: Justin Casey <4348807+justincasey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Model loader: per-rank snapshots of loaded weights

With DSV41_WEIGHT_SNAPSHOT=1, BaseModelLoader.load_model restores the
target model's loaded weights from a per-rank snapshot instead of reading
the checkpoint, and writes one when it has to read the checkpoint.

A snapshot holds the state right after load_weights, before
process_weights_after_loading: every storage behind the model's parameters
and buffers, 4 KiB aligned in one data file, with a manifest (tensor
layout, a CRC32 per 64 MiB chunk, the plain-data attributes load_weights
set, such as disk Engram's file references) and a COMPLETE marker holding
the manifest's SHA-256. A restore builds the model as usual, checks the
layout and replay preconditions, reads the file with O_DIRECT through four
pinned 64 MiB slots into the storages in place, replays the attributes,
and then runs the usual post-processing, which therefore sees bit-identical
inputs and rebuilds every derived tensor, kernel argument and plain
attribute itself. Nothing post-processing produces is ever restored, so
value-dependent processing (the packed BF16 head's exponent base and
exception count, the scaled indexer projection, the MoE repack's K tails)
needs no special handling.

The key covers the checkpoint (shard sizes, mtimes and safetensors headers,
JSON contents), the rank, the vLLM and B12X Python sources, Torch and the
device, VllmConfig.compute_hash() and the resolved HF config, the load
format, the engine environment (VLLM_*, SPARK3_*, B12X_*, DSV41_*,
SAFETENSORS_*, without secrets and ports) and DSV41_WEIGHT_SNAPSHOT_TAG.
Every rank must hold a valid snapshot or every rank loads the checkpoint
(a CPU-group all-reduce); a read or CRC failure on any rank discards that
snapshot and sends every rank to the checkpoint. A snapshot is written only
if load_weights replaced no parameter, buffer or submodule and changed no
attribute other than plain data and parameter-backed tensors. Draft models,
loaders other than DefaultModelLoader's family and online-quantized models
always load the checkpoint. Snapshots live under DSV41_WEIGHT_SNAPSHOT_DIR
(default /cache/dsv41/weight-snapshots), DSV41_WEIGHT_SNAPSHOT_KEEP per rank
(default 1). DSV41_WEIGHT_SNAPSHOT_DIGEST=1 writes per-tensor CRC32 digests
of the processed model (parameters, buffers, attribute tensors) for
comparing a restored boot with a checkpoint boot.

The idea of a per-rank processed-weight snapshot comes from
kindlingai/glm-5.3-flash-gx10 (no code taken).

Tests: tests/model_executor/model_loader/test_weight_snapshot.py (CPU).

License: Apache-2.0 (dsv41-1017 recipe, DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017-4x-DGX-Spark).
